              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you're shopping for a flatbed trailer, there's more to consider than just the sticker price. Whether you're expanding your fleet or replacing a well-worn unit, knowing what impacts the cost can help you make a smart, budget-conscious investment. In this guide, we'll walk through pricing ranges, factors that drive up or lower the cost, and how to choose a trailer that delivers long-term value for your business.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-types",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Different Types of Flatbed Trailers and What Sets Them Apart",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "types"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-types-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not all <a href=\"/store/inventory?type=trailer\">flatbed trailers</a> are built the same, and the type you choose can have a major impact on price, performance, and hauling capacity. Whether you're loading pallets or oversized equipment, it's important to understand the differences so you can invest in the right fit for your freight.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-types-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type4",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Standard Flatbed",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Open deck with no sides or roof, ideal for equipment, lumber, steel coils, and palletized goods. Typically 48′ or 53′ with a deck height around 5 feet.",
                        "tag": "BEST FOR: VERSATILE, GENERAL FREIGHT"
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Gooseneck",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Connects to a hitch in the bed of a pickup or tractor, offering better weight distribution and tighter turning.",
                        "tag": "BEST FOR: HOTSHOT LOADS, TIGHT MANEUVERING"
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Drop Deck (Step Deck)",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Two deck levels, a higher front and lower rear, for hauling taller equipment while staying within legal height limits.",
                        "tag": "BEST FOR: TALL CARGO, CONSTRUCTION EQUIPMENT"
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Extendable Flatbed",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Stretches to accommodate extra-long freight like steel beams or wind turbine blades, then collapses for easy storage.",
                        "tag": "BEST FOR: LONG, OVERSIZED HAULS"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginTop": 8,
                      "marginBottom": 34
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-price-factors",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Factors Affect the Price?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "price-factors"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-price-factors-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The cost of a flatbed trailer isn't fixed. It varies depending on design, materials, features, and more. Here's what can influence your final price tag.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-price-factors-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "stack",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Trailer Size and Type",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Longer trailers or ones with specialized capabilities, such as extendable decks or drop decks, will cost more than basic 48-foot models."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Material and Build Quality",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "<strong>Aluminum:</strong> Lightweight and corrosion-resistant, but typically more expensive."
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "<strong>Steel:</strong> Durable and affordable, but heavier and more prone to rust."
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "<strong>Combo Builds:</strong> A mix of both for balance between weight and cost."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Load Capacity",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Higher weight ratings often require reinforced framing and axles, which increase manufacturing cost."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Add-On Features",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Toolboxes and tie-down points"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Winches and ramps"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Custom flooring or coatings"
                          }
                        ],
                        "outro": "Each feature adds functionality but also increases the price."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginBottom": 8
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-price-factors-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Need a trailer that fits your budget and workload? Browse our selection of new flatbed trailers built for real-world use.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginTop": 34
                    }
                  }
                },
