                        "style": "primary"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-mistakes",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Mistakes to Avoid When Shopping for a Flatbed",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "mistakes"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistakes-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Making the wrong call on a trailer can cost you more down the road. Here are common buying mistakes to steer clear of.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-mistakes-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "mark": "xdot",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Overbuying for Your Needs",
                        "text": "You don't need a top-tier model with every feature if your hauls are local and light-duty. Choose a trailer that suits your routes and cargo."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Ignoring Long-Term Costs",
                        "text": "A cheaper trailer might save money upfront, but lead to higher maintenance costs. Consider the total cost of ownership, not just the purchase price."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Skipping the Inspection (for Used Units)",
                        "text": "If you're buying used, inspect welds, flooring, brakes, and suspension. Make sure everything is in solid working condition."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Not Thinking Ahead",
                        "text": "If your business is growing, invest in a trailer that supports expansion, not just today's needs."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-faqs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "FAQs: Flatbed Trailer Costs and Buying Tips",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "faqs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "questions-faqs-1",
                  "type": "qa-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "q": "How much does a flatbed trailer cost to maintain?",
                        "a": "Maintenance varies, but plan for regular brake checks, tire replacements, and deck inspections."
                      },
                      {
                        "q": "Is it better to lease or buy?",
                        "a": "If you haul consistently and plan to use the trailer for years, buying offers the most value. Leasing works best for short-term or seasonal needs."
                      },
                      {
                        "q": "Should I consider a used trailer?",
                        "a": "Yes, used trailers can be a cost-effective solution if they're well-maintained. Just make sure to verify the condition and service records."
                      },
                      {
                        "q": "What are the most cost-effective brands?",
                        "a": "Look for trailers from reputable manufacturers that offer warranty options and parts availability. Sun State Trailers works with trusted brands that prioritize quality."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-choose-the-right-flatbed",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Choose the Right Flatbed for Your Budget",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-choose-the-right-flatbed-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Price matters, but so does performance. The best flatbed trailer is one that matches your operational needs, keeps your cargo secure, and stays reliable for years to come. At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we help Florida business owners make smart equipment investments with clarity and confidence. Whether you're ready to buy or just weighing your options, our team is here to help you find the right trailer at the right price.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
